WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.260
Welcome to DBL Group’s TalentHub!

2
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.700
This tutorial is specially designed for
the Factory HR team. As a Factory HR user,

3
00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:22.740
you have three main responsibilities
in TalentHub. In this video,

4
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:28.020
we’ll walk through how to complete
each of these tasks. Let’s get started!

5
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.210
First, when a requisition
is created for your unit,

6
00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.970
it comes to the Factory HR team.

7
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:40.809
Your responsibility is to
complete the Job Analysis

8
00:00:40.929 --> 00:00:47.050
before the approval process begins.
Second, once the job is posted,

9
00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:52.090
you can forward collected CVs
to the assigned recruiter.

10
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:58.090
And third, when the recruiter
assigns candidates to you,

11
00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:01.003
you’ll conduct their first interviews.

12
00:01:01.353 --> 00:01:06.193
Now let’s take a closer look at the scope
of your responsibilities as Factory HR.

13
00:01:06.313 --> 00:01:12.353
Approving requisitions, determining
salaries or offers, and managing the

14
00:01:12.473 --> 00:01:17.793
recruiter’s complete candidate pipeline
are outside the scope of this role.

15
00:01:17.913 --> 00:01:21.913
Your primary responsibilities
are completing Job Analysis,

16
00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:27.593
forwarding CVs to the recruiter,
and conducting assigned interviews.

17
00:01:30.443 --> 00:01:35.443
First, let’s understand how
to get Factory HR access.

18
00:01:35.563 --> 00:01:41.042
This role is assigned
separately for each unit.

19
00:01:41.162 --> 00:01:45.763
To obtain Factory HR access for your unit,
contact the Head of Talent Acquisition.

20
00:01:45.883 --> 00:01:51.204
They will arrange the necessary access.
Multiple Factory HR users can be

21
00:01:51.324 --> 00:01:56.763
assigned to the same unit, and they
share the same Job Analysis Queue.

22
00:01:57.113 --> 00:02:01.233
To sign in to TalentHub, use your
official DBL email address and password.

23
00:02:01.353 --> 00:02:05.993
For your first login, your initial
password is your Employee Code.

24
00:02:06.113 --> 00:02:11.713
After signing in, set your own password.

25
00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:17.263
After signing in, you’ll find several
important options in the sidebar.

26
00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:22.503
First is Requisitions, where you’ll
complete Job Analysis. Next is Assigned

27
00:02:22.623 --> 00:02:28.303
Candidates. This option appears when
the recruiter assigns candidates to you.

28
00:02:28.423 --> 00:02:34.383
My Interviews contains information
about interviews you’re involved in.

29
00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:38.783
And next to the notification bell,
you’ll find the Availability button.

30
00:02:38.903 --> 00:02:42.023
You’ll use this when
you’re going on leave.

31
00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:50.673
Let’s start with your first
responsibility: completing the Job

32
00:02:50.793 --> 00:02:56.753
Analysis. When a Requisition Raiser
submits a new requisition for your unit,

33
00:02:56.873 --> 00:03:01.953
all Factory HR users assigned to that
unit receive a notification. Any one

34
00:03:02.073 --> 00:03:08.032
of them can then open the requisition
and begin working on it. To get started,

35
00:03:08.152 --> 00:03:11.902
open Requisitions. Then select the
requisition with the Job Analysis status.

36
00:03:12.023 --> 00:03:17.683
When you open the requisition, you’ll
see the Job Analysis tab. There are two

37
00:03:17.803 --> 00:03:23.023
sections here. Section A contains the
information submitted by the Requisition

38
00:03:23.463 --> 00:03:29.423
Raiser. Section B is where you’ll complete
your work. It contains four fields that

39
00:03:29.783 --> 00:03:34.863
need to be filled in. You’ll also find
Last worked on by, which shows who

40
00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:40.503
most recently worked on the requisition.
This helps avoid duplicate work.

41
00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:46.573
Now suppose you notice incorrect
information in Section A.

42
00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:50.453
In that case,
click Edit vacancy information. From here,

43
00:03:50.573 --> 00:03:56.733
you can correct details such as the
designation, department, position count,

44
00:03:57.093 --> 00:04:01.653
or dates. Any changes you make will
be recorded in the system History.

45
00:04:01.773 --> 00:04:05.013
However, the requisition’s Approval
Chain will remain unchanged.

46
00:04:05.363 --> 00:04:11.323
Now let’s begin preparing
the Job Analysis.

47
00:04:11.443 --> 00:04:17.483
TalentHub includes a special AI-powered
feature to make this process easier.

48
00:04:18.043 --> 00:04:22.683
Notice the Draft With AI button. When you
click it, the system’s AI analyzes the

49
00:04:22.803 --> 00:04:26.923
requisition information and automatically
generates a Job Analysis draft.

50
00:04:27.043 --> 00:04:31.803
It prepares initial content for
all four sections: Job Description,

51
00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:36.283
Education & Training, Experience, and
Others. This means you don’t have to write

52
00:04:36.403 --> 00:04:42.603
everything from scratch. However, always
review the AI-generated content carefully

53
00:04:42.723 --> 00:04:48.003
and make any necessary
adjustments before submitting.

54
00:04:48.353 --> 00:04:53.593
The first field is Job Description.
Here, you’ll describe the main duties

55
00:04:53.713 --> 00:04:59.434
and responsibilities of the position.
Next, use Education & Training to specify

56
00:04:59.554 --> 00:05:05.754
the required qualifications and training.
Under Experience, mention how

57
00:05:05.874 --> 00:05:12.074
many years of experience are needed. And
in Others, you can include any additional

58
00:05:12.194 --> 00:05:16.892
requirements or conditions. Let’s update
the Experience field as an example.

59
00:05:17.242 --> 00:05:21.762
The Job Analysis details have
already been included in the form.

60
00:05:21.882 --> 00:05:26.962
However, if you have any additional
documents relevant to the position,

61
00:05:27.082 --> 00:05:33.363
you can attach them here.
Simply go to the Attachments section

62
00:05:33.483 --> 00:05:35.183
and upload the required PDF files.

63
00:05:35.303 --> 00:05:40.483
Remember, any additional attachments must
be added during the Job Analysis stage.

64
00:05:40.603 --> 00:05:46.042
Once submitted, these files become
part of the approval process.

65
00:05:46.392 --> 00:05:51.472
Suppose you need to stop working on the
Job Analysis for another urgent task.

66
00:05:52.152 --> 00:05:56.832
No problem.
Click Save to keep your progress.

67
00:05:56.952 --> 00:06:02.352
Later, you or another
Factory HR user from your

68
00:06:02.472 --> 00:06:06.232
unit can continue from where you left off.

69
00:06:06.582 --> 00:06:12.462
But what if the requisition contains
an issue that prevents you from

70
00:06:12.582 --> 00:06:18.702
completing the Job Analysis?
In that case, use Return to raiser.

71
00:06:18.822 --> 00:06:24.942
Explain which information needs to be
corrected or added. Then click Send back.

72
00:06:25.902 --> 00:06:31.822
Once the Requisition Raiser makes
the corrections and resubmits,

73
00:06:31.942 --> 00:06:37.131
the requisition returns to
your unit’s Job Analysis Queue.

74
00:06:37.481 --> 00:06:40.391
Once you’ve reviewed all the information
and completed the Job Analysis,

75
00:06:40.511 --> 00:06:44.561
click Submit for approval. The requisition
status will change to Pending Approval.

76
00:06:44.841 --> 00:06:49.202
At the same time,
the first approver in the assigned

77
00:06:49.322 --> 00:06:54.322
Approval Chain will receive a
notification. From this point onward,

78
00:06:54.762 --> 00:06:59.481
the assigned approvers will
handle the approval process.

79
00:06:59.831 --> 00:07:03.781
Here’s another useful thing to know. If
a unit has no assigned Factory HR users,

80
00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:08.111
or all of them are on leave, the Head
of Talent Acquisition and recruiters

81
00:07:08.231 --> 00:07:14.031
can complete the Job Analysis. However,
when Factory HR users are available,

82
00:07:14.671 --> 00:07:19.751
this responsibility remains
with the Factory HR team.

83
00:07:22.601 --> 00:07:28.161
Now let’s move to your
second responsibility:

84
00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:33.641
sending CVs to the recruiter. Once
the recruiter publishes a job posting,

85
00:07:33.761 --> 00:07:39.801
the Profile & Posting tab will display
the Send CVs to the recruiter option.

86
00:07:39.921 --> 00:07:46.161
You’ll also find the public job link here.
Use Share job link to send it to others.

87
00:07:46.921 --> 00:07:51.961
And under Social post, you’ll find
ready-to-share content for Facebook.

88
00:07:52.311 --> 00:07:58.151
Suppose you’ve collected CVs from
several candidates for this position.

89
00:07:58.271 --> 00:08:03.831
First, select the Source. This indicates
where the CVs were collected from.

90
00:08:03.951 --> 00:08:09.833
If they came through Employee Referral,
select that option.

91
00:08:09.953 --> 00:08:14.871
You’ll then need to provide
the referrer’s information.

92
00:08:15.221 --> 00:08:19.421
After selecting the Source,
upload the candidates’ CVs.

93
00:08:19.541 --> 00:08:25.741
You can upload up to thirty PDF files at
a time. The system automatically attempts

94
00:08:25.861 --> 00:08:31.381
to identify candidate names from the
filenames. If any name is incorrect,

95
00:08:31.501 --> 00:08:37.621
correct it before proceeding. Once you’ve
verified everything, click Send CVs.

96
00:08:37.971 --> 00:08:42.891
After submission, the CVs are added to the
recruiter’s pipeline with Applied status.

97
00:08:43.771 --> 00:08:48.091
The system also records
that you submitted them.

98
00:08:48.851 --> 00:08:53.691
In the list below, you can see
which candidates you’ve forwarded.

99
00:08:54.451 --> 00:08:59.611
You’ll also see how many times
they’ve applied previously.

100
00:09:00.451 --> 00:09:06.291
However, the assigned recruiter decides
which candidates will be shortlisted.

101
00:09:09.141 --> 00:09:13.101
Now let’s move to your
third responsibility:

102
00:09:13.221 --> 00:09:18.741
conducting first interviews.
When the recruiter uses Send for interview

103
00:09:18.861 --> 00:09:24.021
to assign candidates to you,
you’ll receive a notification.

104
00:09:24.141 --> 00:09:28.301
The Assigned Candidates option
will also appear in your menu.

105
00:09:28.741 --> 00:09:33.181
Here, you’ll see only the
candidates assigned to you.

106
00:09:33.301 --> 00:09:36.981
The recruiter’s full candidate
pipeline won’t be visible.

107
00:09:37.331 --> 00:09:43.371
The Assigned Candidates
page contains five columns.

108
00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:49.427
First is To schedule, for candidates whose
interviews haven’t been scheduled yet.

109
00:09:49.547 --> 00:09:53.042
Scheduled means an interview date
and time have been set.

110
00:09:53.162 --> 00:09:58.411
Decision due means the
interview is complete,

111
00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:04.971
but a decision is still pending.

112
00:10:05.251 --> 00:10:08.491
With HR Head means the candidate
is awaiting HR Head review.

113
00:10:09.251 --> 00:10:13.731
And Done means the relevant
process has been completed.

114
00:10:14.081 --> 00:10:20.001
Now let’s see how to schedule interviews.
Suppose you want to interview

115
00:10:20.121 --> 00:10:25.561
two candidates on the same day.
Select the checkboxes next to their names.

116
00:10:25.761 --> 00:10:31.562
Then click Schedule 2 selected.
If you don’t select anyone individually,

117
00:10:31.682 --> 00:10:37.201
you can use Schedule all to
schedule all candidates together.

118
00:10:37.551 --> 00:10:40.631
Now select the interview date and time.

119
00:10:41.271 --> 00:10:46.951
All interview times follow Bangladesh
Standard Time, or GMT Plus Six.

120
00:10:47.631 --> 00:10:51.911
For online interviews, the system
automatically generates a Google

121
00:10:52.031 --> 00:10:57.991
Meet link. For in-person interviews,
select the appropriate Location.

122
00:10:58.511 --> 00:11:02.511
Then specify the interview room.

123
00:11:02.861 --> 00:11:06.761
Next, select the interview panel members.
The panel is divided into two groups.

124
00:11:06.881 --> 00:11:12.341
The first is From HR Department.
The second is From other departments.

125
00:11:12.461 --> 00:11:18.478
The HR panelist will also
complete the candidate’s Salary

126
00:11:18.598 --> 00:11:24.521
and Benefits information in the form.

127
00:11:24.641 --> 00:11:29.461
Below, you’ll see how candidates
and panel members will be notified.

128
00:11:29.581 --> 00:11:34.981
Candidates receive Google Calendar and
Email notifications. For panel members,

129
00:11:35.101 --> 00:11:41.021
there’s the Notify option.
Once everything is ready, click Schedule.

130
00:11:41.371 --> 00:11:44.171
On the interview day,

131
00:11:44.291 --> 00:11:48.499
each candidate card displays
an important question.

132
00:11:48.619 --> 00:11:53.994
Did this interview happen?

133
00:11:54.114 --> 00:12:00.091
If the candidate attended,
select Interviewed.

134
00:12:00.211 --> 00:12:05.891
If they didn’t attend,
select Did not attend.

135
00:12:06.011 --> 00:12:11.451
If you select the wrong option,
use Undo to correct it.

136
00:12:11.571 --> 00:12:17.661
However, once a panel
member has entered a score,

137
00:12:17.781 --> 00:12:19.681
Did not attend is no longer available.

138
00:12:19.801 --> 00:12:25.681
If you need to change an interview date
or time, use Reschedule.

139
00:12:25.801 --> 00:12:29.161
You can select the new date
and time from here. The candidate

140
00:12:29.281 --> 00:12:33.121
will receive both the original
and updated schedule details by email.

141
00:12:33.241 --> 00:12:37.441
The interview links for panel members
will remain unchanged. However,

142
00:12:37.561 --> 00:12:42.281
once a panel member submits a score, the
interview can no longer be rescheduled.

143
00:12:42.631 --> 00:12:46.031
Now let’s look at candidate
assessment scores.

144
00:12:46.151 --> 00:12:51.071
TalentHub supports three
types of assessments.

145
00:12:51.191 --> 00:12:57.071
These are Written Test, Computer
Literacy Test, and AI Proficiency Test.

146
00:12:57.191 --> 00:13:02.511
Enter the scores for whichever
assessments apply to the candidate.

147
00:13:03.111 --> 00:13:09.391
Remember, once you submit a score,
it becomes locked for you.

148
00:13:09.511 --> 00:13:14.271
If a correction is needed later,

149
00:13:14.391 --> 00:13:17.831
contact the assigned recruiter
or the Head of Talent Acquisition.

150
00:13:18.181 --> 00:13:23.341
Once the panel evaluation is complete,
the candidate moves to the Decision

151
00:13:23.461 --> 00:13:28.501
due column. Now it’s time to
make a decision. Click Decide.

152
00:13:28.621 --> 00:13:33.501
The main question is whether the
candidate should move to the next stage.

153
00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:39.661
If you select Yes, the candidate goes to
your unit’s HR Head, if one is assigned.

154
00:13:39.781 --> 00:13:45.541
Otherwise, the candidate moves
directly to the Final stage.

155
00:13:45.891 --> 00:13:50.731
If you don’t want the candidate
to proceed, select No.

156
00:13:50.851 --> 00:13:56.291
You’ll need to provide a
reason for your decision.

157
00:13:56.411 --> 00:14:01.910
The reason will also be visible to
the relevant people in later stages.

158
00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:07.851
You’ll find an option called Also
send the regret mail. If selected,

159
00:14:08.071 --> 00:14:12.171
DBL Group’s Regret Letter will be sent to
the candidate. Remember, this email isn’t

160
00:14:12.291 --> 00:14:16.771
sent automatically. It’s sent only once,
when you explicitly select the option.

161
00:14:17.121 --> 00:14:22.681
Suppose you’ve selected several
candidates to move forward.

162
00:14:22.801 --> 00:14:29.081
In that case, you can use Send finalists
to HR Head. The HR Head will receive a

163
00:14:29.201 --> 00:14:35.001
single email containing the list of
selected candidates. They can approve

164
00:14:35.121 --> 00:14:40.601
the candidates directly from that email.
If any candidate is returned for

165
00:14:40.721 --> 00:14:45.601
reconsideration, they’ll come back to
you along with the HR Head’s comments.

166
00:14:48.451 --> 00:14:53.331
Now let’s see how to update your
Availability when you’re going on leave.

167
00:14:53.451 --> 00:14:58.571
Next to the notification bell,
you’ll find a round button.

168
00:14:58.691 --> 00:15:04.091
Green means you’re Available.

169
00:15:04.211 --> 00:15:08.811
Amber means you’re Away.
To set your leave, click the button.

170
00:15:08.931 --> 00:15:13.771
You can choose three days, seven days,
fifteen days, or select a custom end date.

171
00:15:13.891 --> 00:15:18.771
You can also add a note if needed.
Then click Confirm leave.

172
00:15:19.121 --> 00:15:25.400
Now let’s see what changes after
you set your status to Away.

173
00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:30.761
You’ll temporarily leave
the Job Analysis Queue.

174
00:15:31.601 --> 00:15:37.401
You won’t receive new Job
Analysis notifications.

175
00:15:37.521 --> 00:15:41.271
Pending Job Analysis items will
also disappear from your list.

176
00:15:41.391 --> 00:15:45.160
However, other available Factory HR
users in your unit can continue the work.

177
00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:48.471
If nobody is available, the Head of
Talent Acquisition will handle it.

178
00:15:48.591 --> 00:15:53.271
Suppose you return from
leave earlier than expected.

179
00:15:53.391 --> 00:15:58.311
Simply click the Availability button
and select I’m back.

180
00:15:59.151 --> 00:16:04.231
Your status will change to Available
again. If you don’t make any changes,

181
00:16:04.351 --> 00:16:08.751
the system automatically restores your
availability on the scheduled end date.

182
00:16:09.101 --> 00:16:14.341
Now let’s understand what information is
available to you as a Factory HR user.

183
00:16:14.461 --> 00:16:19.194
You can view Job Analysis requisitions
for your unit. You can also access

184
00:16:19.314 --> 00:16:25.221
posted requisitions to forward CVs. And
you’ll see the candidates assigned to you.

185
00:16:25.341 --> 00:16:30.821
However, this role doesn’t provide
access to other users’ complete candidate

186
00:16:30.941 --> 00:16:35.079
pipelines, salary decisions,
or onboarding information.

187
00:16:37.929 --> 00:16:41.729
Now let’s see when you’ll
receive notifications. You’ll be

188
00:16:42.329 --> 00:16:48.089
notified when a new requisition from
your unit is waiting for Job Analysis.

189
00:16:48.209 --> 00:16:53.169
You’ll also receive an update when a
Requisition Raiser corrects and resubmits

190
00:16:53.689 --> 00:16:59.409
a requisition. Notifications are sent when
the recruiter assigns candidates to you.

191
00:16:59.529 --> 00:17:05.329
You’ll also be updated when the HR Head
approves, returns, or rejects a candidate.

192
00:17:05.449 --> 00:17:11.049
And you’ll receive notifications when your
interviews are scheduled or rescheduled.

193
00:17:11.399 --> 00:17:17.159
You can view these notifications through
the bell icon at the top. You can also

194
00:17:17.279 --> 00:17:21.229
receive them by email. To enable this,
open Settings and go to the Notifications

195
00:17:21.349 --> 00:17:26.599
tab. Keep Email notifications turned on to
receive important updates in your inbox.

196
00:17:29.449 --> 00:17:35.249
Now let’s answer a few
frequently asked questions.

197
00:17:35.369 --> 00:17:40.609
Suppose one of your colleagues has already
started a Job Analysis. Can you finish it?

198
00:17:41.369 --> 00:17:46.849
Yes, you can. Any Factory HR user assigned
to the same unit can complete the work.

199
00:17:46.969 --> 00:17:53.409
Last worked on by shows who
most recently worked on it.

200
00:17:53.689 --> 00:17:57.369
And the detailed change history
is recorded in the system.

201
00:17:57.719 --> 00:18:03.599
Another question: why can’t you attach new
files after submitting the Job Analysis?

202
00:18:03.719 --> 00:18:06.969
Because submitted attachments
become part of the approval process.

203
00:18:07.089 --> 00:18:10.859
If you need to add another file,

204
00:18:10.979 --> 00:18:16.479
contact the Head of Talent Acquisition.

205
00:18:16.599 --> 00:18:21.759
Similarly, if you need to correct an
assessment score you’ve submitted,

206
00:18:21.919 --> 00:18:26.679
contact the assigned recruiter or the
Head of Talent Acquisition for assistance.

207
00:18:29.529 --> 00:18:33.649
Let’s quickly recap your
three main responsibilities.

208
00:18:33.769 --> 00:18:39.329
First, open Requisitions to
complete the Job Analysis.

209
00:18:39.449 --> 00:18:43.649
Use Draft With AI to
generate an initial draft,

210
00:18:43.769 --> 00:18:48.329
review the information,
and click Submit for approval.

211
00:18:48.679 --> 00:18:54.879
Second, open Profile & Posting
to forward CVs to the recruiter.

212
00:18:54.999 --> 00:19:01.239
Select the Source and upload the
candidates’ PDFs. Then click Send CVs.

213
00:19:01.589 --> 00:19:06.829
Third, open Assigned Candidates
to manage interviews.

214
00:19:06.949 --> 00:19:09.709
Schedule the interviews,
confirm attendance,

215
00:19:09.829 --> 00:19:14.789
and record your decision
after the evaluation.

216
00:19:15.139 --> 00:19:19.339
And remember to update your
Availability before going on leave.

217
